ors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 5 1500X Quad-Core Processor (8 threads) - 31.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf an OptionButton is scaled, its child PopupMenu doesn't follow its scale.\n\nI am working on a pixelart game where I scale all my UI x2, x3 etc. based on settings/resolution. This works as expected except for the OptionButton where the items in the PopupMenu stay at x1 scale:\n\n<img width=\"555\" height=\"134\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/25401891-9ed3-401a-82b3-5fc8c7789d52\" />\n\n\nI attempted to mitigate by overriding the font size by code, but I would also need to handle the separation, the icon and possibly more...  I do believe instead the PopupMenu matching the scale of its parent OptionButton should be the default behaviour.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n<img width=\"373\" height=\"289\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d56e1c68-0fb1-4cde-a3d9-ab7b2f28b32e\" />\n\nOpen MRP, click on the OptionsButton, observe mismatching scale of items.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[options-button-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27308549/options-button-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ma